{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S1 T1 vivacious-widish-indianabat (2c81) CLAIMED (epic + S1 mica-governing-buck claimed first; all three were already certified). PHASE 4a CENSUS: T1 is a deliberately pre-cutover internal unit (file_impact is binding_repository.py + its test only, and the ticket's Out-of-scope names facade delegation). Surface slots: CLI = out of scope (internal module, unreachable until T2 cutover); MCP/API tool = out of scope (same); library facade public import path = out of scope BY TICKET DESIGN, T2 evadable-curious-mastodon proves BindingStore facade parity; automated callers (reconciler) = out of scope, reached only after T2; dual-direction read-vs-write = IN SCOPE and proven (load and save both characterized for live, retired, and rotation files). Contention triggers: EXEMPT - T1 adds no lock composition, no retry/backoff, and no cache; it characterizes an existing single save seam. PHASE 4b RED EVIDENCE: authored 27 direct-repository tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py; all 27 collect and fail with NotImplementedError against a signature-only scaffold, i.e. genuine absence of behavior rather than an import error (a bare-missing-module ImportError was rejected as invalid RED and replaced with the scaffold). Existing-coverage inventory first (test-design section 1): rotation-failure and two-save convergence are ALREADY fully covered for BindingStore in state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py, so the new tests prove those contracts through the NEW owner rather than duplicating; rows with no prior coverage anywhere were no-eager-write-on-construction, retired-file write failure, retire-time live-replace failure, and alert-persistence failure. PHASE 4c HOLD-OUT: 15 fault/corruption tests physically moved OUT of the worktree to /tmp/rp02-heldout/T1_FULL_test_binding_repository.py; only the 12 happy-path tests remain in tree for the implementer."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787095421037421001,"uuid":"d6c7240c-357e-4fd8-b9d9-7a82fef0b79c"}